 ## Capture Behavior
 
 - A session ID is generated from local date and time using `yyyyMMdd_HHmmss_SSS`.
-- A campaign ID is generated as `sipobs_YYYYMMDD` on first use and retained across blocks, app restarts, and later days until edited.
+- A campaign ID is generated as `sipobs_YYYYMMDD` on first use and retained internally. No campaign or condition typing is required.
+- New sessions use their generated session ID for both `conditionLabel` and the compatible `scenarioId` alias. Existing unfinished sessions retain their original metadata when restored. Pair caller/target recordings using session records and timestamps; these automatic IDs do not synchronize the phones.
 - The session ID is also used as the JSON filename.
 - Fused high-accuracy location is requested approximately once per second.
 - The foreground service requests one radio/environment sample per second independently of fused location callbacks. Indoor location silence does not stop Cell recording.
